From 7a7591117e31c6c4c73dda9de9b620dbf1f9d23b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: palazik <gochmyradov0@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:02:09 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] dodge: early framebuffer debug markers (find where XNU dies
 before kprintf)

Port of dipa-studio/ios-sweet 0010, with dodge's panel (fb 0xd5100000, 1264x2780,
stride 5056) instead of sweet's.

On device the shim now hands over a correctly loaded kernel (VERIFY insn matched)
but XNU produces no output at all and never clears the screen: it dies or hangs
before serial_init brings up the console, and kprintf is a no-op until
STARTUP_SUB_KPRINTF, so there is nothing to see.

This writes directly to the splash framebuffer long before any console exists:
- start.s: a white band at the bottom as soon as start_first_cpu is reached (MMU
  off, direct store), and one extra Normal-NC block for the framebuffer added to
  the existing V=P L2 so it stays reachable with the bootstrap MMU on.
- osfmk/arm64/dodge_early.c: no allocation, no locks, no ADT - usable before any
  per-CPU or thread state exists. Draws 'DODGE EARLY <n>' plus a colored stage band.
- arm_init: markers 1-7 (entered, PE_init_platform, cpu topology, cpu_bootstrap,
  startup_bootstrap, cpu_init, entering arm_vm_init).
- arm_vm_init: dodge_early_disable() before the bootstrap TTBR0 is torn down,
  since the V=P framebuffer mapping belongs to the outgoing table.
- panic_trap_to_debugger: print the panic string early, before the normal path
  needs CPU/thread state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 osfmk/arm/arm_init.c      |   9 +++
 osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c |   3 +
 osfmk/arm64/dodge_early.c | 130 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 osfmk/arm64/dodge_early.h |  22 +++++++
 osfmk/arm64/start.s       |  36 +++++++++++
 osfmk/conf/files.arm64    |   1 +
 osfmk/kern/debug.c        |   8 +++
 7 files changed, 209 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 osfmk/arm64/dodge_early.c
 create mode 100644 osfmk/arm64/dodge_early.h

